elihood, severity, or operating thresholds of the resulting defects.\"},{\"summary\":\"Inclusion-shape control is a mitigation process\",\"explanation\":\"Inclusion-shape control converts elongated or flattened sulphide inclusions, particularly MnS, into more globular inclusions. The stated purpose is to eliminate flattened MnS inclusions that can trigger separation initiation and thereby reduce separation-related defects [Data: Entities (700); Relationships (930)].\\n\\nThis process is connected to the broader sulphide-shape control technique and is described as being achieved through additions of rare-earth metals and/or calcium [Data: Entities (700, 762); Relationships (996)].\"},{\"summary\":\"Desulphurization provides a separate sulfur-reduction pathway\",\"explanation\":\"Desulphurization is described as a sulphide-shape-control-related method that reduces sulfur content to an extremely low level. Sulfur is explicitly identified as the element represented by S [Data: Entities (742, 745)].\\n\\nThe relationship between desulphurization and sulfur reduction is direct, but the supplied data do not establish that desulphurization alone eliminates all separation initiation mechanisms [Data: Relationships (975)].\"},{\"summary\":\"Separation has distinct initiation and propagation stages\",\"explanation\":\"The community distinguishes separation initiation from separation propagation. Initiation is the stage at which separation begins, including initiation triggered by flattened MnS inclusions [Data: Entities (763, 727)].\\n\\nAfter initiation, separation tends to propagate along the material’s banded structure. This creates a sequential process in which the initiating defect and the subsequent propagation path are related but distinct phenomena [Data: Entities (764); Relationships (999, 1000)].\"},{\"summary\":\"Chemical composition and hot-rolling condition may alter initiation mechanisms\",\"explanation\":\"The mechanism responsible for separation crack initiatio